      'Because the whole Year 4 cohort sits the test together as a normal part of the school term, most children don\'t feel unusual pressure on the day — for many, it feels similar to any other classroom activity. There\'s no need for special stationery or preparation beyond a good night\'s sleep and a relaxed morning.',
      'Results aren\'t shared as a score or ranking. Families of selected students are simply notified by the school that their child has been invited to join the PEAC program, usually later in the year. If your child isn\'t selected, there is no notification and nothing to worry about — PEAC is one of many ways schools support learners, not a measure of overall ability.',
