      "South Australia's IGNITE program is one of the state's most sought-after pathways for academically able students, giving high-achieving learners access to accelerated, extension-rich classes from Year 7 onward. Three schools currently host IGNITE classes — Glenunga International High School in the inner south-east, Aberfoyle Park High School in the southern suburbs, and The Heights School in the northern suburbs — each running its own intake but drawing on the same entrance testing process. Because places are limited and demand is high each year, families across metropolitan Adelaide and beyond apply, making the entrance test a genuinely competitive hurdle rather than a formality.",
