    shortName: 'HAST',
    state: 'National (NSW, VIC, QLD, SA, WA)',
    yearLevel: 'Years 5–12 (Primary and Secondary levels)',
    color: '#D97706',
    lightBg: '#FFFBEB',
    icon: '🏆',
    metaTitle: 'HAST Test Preparation | ACER Higher Ability Selection Test Practice',
    metaDesc: 'Prepare for the ACER HAST with practice in Reading, Maths Reasoning, Abstract Reasoning and Writing. Used by 100+ selective and independent schools across Australia.',
    keywords: 'HAST test, HAST preparation, ACER HAST, Higher Ability Selection Test, HAST practice test, HAST Primary, HAST Secondary, selective school entry',
    heroLine: 'The gold standard for selective school entry across Australia.',
    intro: 'The Higher Ability Selection Test (HAST) is ACER\'s flagship cognitive ability test, used by more than 100 selective and independent schools across NSW, VIC, QLD, SA and WA. It assesses reasoning and thinking skills rather than curriculum knowledge, and is available at Primary level (Year 5–6 entry) and three Secondary levels (Junior, Middle, Senior). All HAST assessments are paper-based.',
    introParagraphs: [
      'If your child is applying to a selective or independent school anywhere outside NSW\'s state-run selective system, there is a strong chance the entry test they sit is ACER\'s Higher Ability Selection Test, better known as HAST. Unlike a single, uniform exam, HAST is a suite of four cognitive ability tests — Primary, Junior Secondary, Middle Secondary and Senior Secondary — that ACER licenses to individual schools. More than 100 selective and independent schools across five states use one or more HAST levels as part of their enrolment process, which makes it, by sheer reach, the most widely used school-entry cognitive test in the country.',
      'Because each school buys its own combination of components from ACER, no two HAST sittings look exactly alike. One school might test Reading, Maths Reasoning and Abstract Reasoning in a single morning; another might add Written Expression as a fourth component, or run it on a separate afternoon. What stays constant across every version is the underlying philosophy: HAST is designed to measure how a student thinks, reasons and problem-solves, not what they have memorised from a textbook. That is deliberate — ACER built HAST to reduce the advantage that comes purely from coaching on content, and to give schools a fairer read on a student\'s underlying ability, including for students from non-English-speaking backgrounds who may be disadvantaged by heavily language-based tests.',
      'HAST is also, notably, a paper-based test at every level. In an era where most other selective and scholarship assessments have moved online, sitting HAST still means a booklet, a pencil, and — for the Written Expression component — a pen and lined paper, marked by two independent human assessors rather than a machine. That has real implications for preparation: handwriting speed and stamina matter, filling in bubble-style answer sheets accurately under time pressure is a skill in itself, and students benefit from rehearsing with paper rather than screens. This page walks through what each HAST component actually asks of students, what a good preparation plan looks like across the weeks before the test, and where a full-length practice test can help you find out exactly where your child stands right now.',
    ],
    schools: ['100+ selective and independent schools across 5 states', 'Including Brisbane State High and many independent schools'],
