      "Most Australian schools that participate run ICAS sometime between Term 2 and Term 3, though the exact weeks vary by subject and by school, since each institution books its own sitting dates within the broader ICAS calendar. Students should check with their school for the specific dates their year level and chosen subjects will be tested, as this is set by the school rather than by the family.",
      "Results and award certificates are usually returned to schools some weeks after the testing window closes, and schools then distribute individual results and any High Distinction, Distinction, Credit, Merit or Participation certificates to students directly. Because there is no pass/fail outcome, there is nothing to appeal or resit — the result is simply a benchmark of where a student's skills sat against peers internationally that year.",
